{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '316,330p' STATUS.md\"","aggregated_output":"## Tracked-forward items from WP-SCP-024 024B-core / 024B-extras\n\n- **FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001** (open): per-repo dispatcher install pattern resolved in ACC. install_acc_hook.sh currently hardcodes ROOT_DIR via BASH_SOURCE so each adopter repo would need its own install ceremony. 024C MUST NOT open until closed. ACC-side work item; SCP-side awaits closure. Owner: @jrnb2024.\n- **FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001** (closed in fix-round-4; this commit): 024B-extras workflow wiring now skips script invocation entirely for tooling slices, so the residual operator-supplied `not applicable` bypass surface is gone without passing `--allow-not-applicable` or `--tooling-slice-id` into the script. Cohort cascade slices still invoke the script with full enforcement; defense-in-depth now comes from the workflow short-circuit plus the script's default refusal of `--allow-not-applicable`.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-POLICY-CHECK-TARGET-FILTER-TESTS-001** (open): add per-test coverage for `lib/policy_check_invocation.sh` target-selection loop in 024B-extras-2 (or a future slice). The loop now has 2 path-based excludes (`tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/*` + the narrowed `docs/reviews/*/r1-*.json` + siblings); no direct tests exercise these. Surfaced by R23 fix-round-23 + R24 review of fix-round-24. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001** (open): extend PUT-body shape assertions (`jq -e 'has($field) and .[$field] | type == \"boolean\"'` pattern) across ALL existing restore test cases in `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh`. Fix-round-22 added shape assertions only for the new `restore-getshape-subresources` test; the older restore tests still trust the fake-gh PUT-body acceptance without strict-shape checks. Surfaced by step-7 demo + R22 + R25 against real GitHub API (the 3rd mock-masking CRIT in this slice's history). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001** (closed 2026-05-11): --restore real-repo round-trip evidence at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md` — operator-interactive demo at dispatch-plan step 7 completed against `jrnb2024/scp-024b-extras-restore-test` throw-away repo. **Surfaced CRIT** (mock-masking: transform did not unwrap `*.enabled` sub-objects for `required_linear_history`/`allow_force_pushes`/etc → HTTP 422 on real PUT); closed in fix-round-22 with generic `{enabled: bool}` unwrap + PUT-body-shape assertion test. Round-trip succeeded post-fix; all 4 key fields matched state-A target. Throw-away repo cleanup deferred — current gh token lacks `delete_repo` scope.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-PATH-CONTAINMENT-001** (open): apply `resolve_inside_repo_root()` guard to `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <path>` argument in 024B-extras-2 alongside other defensive hardening. Low blast-radius (operator-credentials-bound). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-COHORT-REGEX-MULTICHAR-001** (open): widen `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` cohort regex from `024[C-F]/` to `024[C-F][^/]*/` for future multi-char cohort slice IDs. Current 5-cohort set (024C/D/E/F) is single-char and unaffected; defensive. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-STEP7-FIXTURE-SEQ-001** (open): align DISPATCH-NOTE step-7 fixture sequence with `restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md` (add or harmonise `Mutate branch protection` step description). Will be resolved naturally at step-7 demo execution time.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-STAGED-RESTORE-TEST-001** (open): add test case for staged-but-uncommitted prior-restore evidence in 024B-extras-2 tests (guards against future narrowing of `git diff HEAD` to `git diff`). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ